# What leaves this machine for Google Cloud to build from - read by both
# `gcloud builds submit` (deploy/deploy.sh) and `gcloud run deploy --source .`
# (deploy/cloudrun.sh). An allow-list, like .dockerignore: nothing personal can
# be sent by being forgotten here.
#
# See exactly what would be sent, without sending it:
#     gcloud meta list-files-for-upload
*
!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore
!requirements.txt
!wsgi.py
!gunicorn.conf.py
!test-report.json
!metermatters/
!metermatters/**

# The pipeline tests before it builds, so the tests travel with the code, along
# with the invented fixtures they read and the scripts that are the pipeline's
# steps. None of it reaches the image: .dockerignore, an allow-list of its own,
# stops it there, and deploy/ci/image.sh checks the image before it is pushed.
#
# Your own fixtures sit directly in tests/fixtures/, and deploy/cloudrun.env
# directly in deploy/. To gcloud, un-ignoring a folder un-ignores everything in
# it - unlike git - so each of the two is opened, emptied again, and only then
# is the one subfolder that may travel let back in. The order of these lines is
# what keeps your files here. deploy/deploy.sh checks the result before every
# upload and refuses to send anything else.
!tests/
!tests/**
tests/fixtures/*
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/
!tests/fixtures/synthetic/**
!deploy/
deploy/*
!deploy/ci/
__pycache__/
